,p_page_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#'
,p_protection_level=>'C'
,p_page_component_map=>'13'
,p_created_on=>wwv_flow_imp.dz('20260831101239Z')
,p_last_updated_on=>wwv_flow_imp.dz('20260901094216Z')
,p_created_by=>'ARCHIPATEL2632004@GMAIL.COM'
,p_last_updated_by=>'ARCHIPATEL2632004@GMAIL.COM'
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(28667885090407215248)
,p_plug_name=>'About'
,p_static_id=>'about'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:t-Region--scrollBody'
,p_plug_template=>4073835273271169698
,p_plug_display_sequence=>10
,p_plug_item_display_point=>'ABOVE'
,p_location=>null
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p><strong>Oracle APEX offers two primary methods for data loading: developer-level administration via the SQL Workshop Data Workshop, and end-user data loading natively integrated into application pages.</strong></p>',
'<p>The modern data loading framework supports file uploads in <strong>CSV, XLSX, XML, and JSON formats,</strong> handling up to <strong>300 columns</strong> concurrently.</p>',
'<h4>1. Developer Tool: The Data Workshop</h4>',
'<p>Developers use this method to quickly seed tables, create new tables from files, or fetch information straight into the database schema.</p>',
'<ul>',
'    <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Navigate to <strong>SQL Workshop > Utilities > Data Workshop.</strong></li>',
'    <li><strong>File Options:</strong> Drag and drop files or choose the <strong>Load from Cloud</strong> option to pull data from a cloud Object Store.</li>',
'    <li><strong>Target Actions:</strong> Choose to insert the raw source into a brand new table or select an existing backend table.</li>',
'    <li><strong>Configuration:</strong> Tweak custom parameters like file encodin, column delimiters, header row identification, and custom null-value strings (e.g., "N/A").</li>',
'</ul>',
'<h4>2. End-User Tool: Application Data Loading</h4>',
'<p>To let end-users securely upload data spreadsheets right from an active runtime application, you must define a programmatic or declarative framework using <strong>Data Load Definitions.</strong></p>',
'<h4>Step A: Create a Data Load Definition</h4>',
'<ol>',
'    <li>Open your application and click on <strong>Shared Components.</strong></li>',
'    <li>Under Data Sources (or Other Components), click <strong>Data Load definitions.</strong></li>',
'    <li>Click <strong>Create</strong> and select your target destination table.</li>',
'    <li>Map your spreadsheet column headers to database table fields. This setup removes mapping responsibility from end users.</li>',
'    <li>Define rules for data transformation or lookup configurations if structure=al modifications are needed.</li>',
'</ol>',
'<h4>Step B: Implement the Front-End Page</h4>',
'<ul>',
'    <li><strong>Declarative Native Method:</strong> Run the Data Load Definition wizard and select the choice to create the processing pages automatically. This creates a standrd file browser container, a preview workspace region, and a processing pa'
||'ge.</li>',
'    <li><strong>Programmatic PL/SQL Method:</strong> Create a custom File Upload item page element and write a specialized process utilizing the APEX_DATA_LOADING.LOAD_DATA API to ingest the BLOB file content into your workspace.</li>',
'</ul>',
''))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
,p_created_on=>wwv_flow_imp.dz('20260901054209Z')
,p_updated_on=>wwv_flow_imp.dz('20260901071517Z')
,p_created_by=>'ARCHIPATEL2632004@GMAIL.COM'
,p_updated_by=>'ARCHIPATEL2632004@GMAIL.COM'
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(32984664808192482935)
,p_plug_name=>'Data Loading'
,p_static_id=>'data'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#'
,p_plug_template=>2675494171183407654
,p_plug_display_sequence=>10
